{
  "id": "Lyo.Authentication.Entra",
  "name": "Lyo.Authentication.Entra",
  "area": "Security",
  "tagline": "Microsoft Entra SAML profile. Federation metadata includes the appid query. Request verification and assertion encryption stay off.",
  "description": "Microsoft Entra SAML profile for `Lyo.Authentication.Saml`. Provider name `entra`, configuration section `EntraAuth`. This profile does not register an OpenID Connect client.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddEntraProvider(o =>\n{\n    o.TenantId = \"tenant-guid\";\n    o.ApplicationId = \"app-guid\";\n    o.EntityId = \"https://api.example.com/saml\";\n    o.AcsUrl = \"https://api.example.com/auth/callback/entra\";\n});"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "Metadata and subject",
      "items": [
        "The metadata URL is `https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenantId}/federationmetadata/2007-06/federationmetadata.xml?appid={applicationId}`. The `appid` query selects that app's token-signing certificate.",
        "The expected issuer is `https://sts.windows.net/{tenantId}/` with the trailing slash.",
        "The subject is `http://schemas.microsoft.com/identity/claims/objectidentifier` when that attribute is present. The email attribute is exactly `http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/emailaddress`.",
        "In the Entra enterprise app, the Identifier must match `EntityId` and the Reply URL must match `AcsUrl`. Leave request verification off and assertion encryption off."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "links": [],
